---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy — CITY JAM" description="We do not sell your data and we never wanted a profile of you." path="/privacy">
  <header class="hero dark bg-band">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="kick"><span class="dot"></span> Privacy · last updated 10 October 2026</p>
      <h1>What we know<br />about <em>you</em>.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Short answer: as little as the thing you asked for requires. We are a music magazine, not an advertising business.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap narrow legal">
      <div class="note"><b>We do not sell your data. We do not run ad networks on you. We do not build a profile of you to rent out.</b> We collect what we need to send you the thing you asked for and to listen to your music properly.</div>
      <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>CITY JAM is the data controller for the information described here. The company number, registered address and a named contact will be added when the legal entity is settled. They are not invented on this page.</p>
      <h2>2. What we collect, and why</h2>
      <p>On this website we do not run a form that stores what you type. The buttons that say apply, join or send open an intake hosted by Perspective, once that intake has a public address. Until it does, the button stays on a page that stores nothing.</p>
      <p>When an intake is open, the fields are the ones that intake asks for. We do not ask this website to collect a phone number. We do not ask for follower counts, and we would not use them if you sent them.</p>
      <h2>3. Who else touches it</h2>
      <p>These are the processors the architecture uses. Each does a specific job and is not permitted to use your data for its own advertising.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Perspective</b> hosts the intake. The site links to it. It does not run on the consumer pages as a tracker.</li>
        <li><b>Nutshell</b> receives consumer signups after Perspective, including Music Ambassador applications, Labs applications, and the business enquiries.</li>
        <li><b>HubSpot</b> (portal 52101795) receives magazine signups after Perspective. The Maestro waitlist is sent to both HubSpot and Nutshell.</li>
        <li><b>beehiiv</b> sends the magazine from <a href="https://dispatch.joinourjam.com">the dispatch</a>.</li>
        <li><b>Vercel</b> hosts this website.</li>
        <li><b>INDUSTRY.AIFF</b> uses its own intake and its own letter. It is not mixed into the consumer lists above.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not use a payment processor. Stripe is not one of these, because this site does not take payment. If that changes, the processor will be named here first.</p>
      <p><b>We do not sell or rent your data to anyone, for any purpose, at any price.</b></p>
      <h2>4. Cookies</h2>
      <p>This site does not set advertising or tracking cookies. If we add analytics, it will be a privacy-preserving one, it will be listed here, and you will be asked first.</p>
      <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Submissions we did not take further</b> are kept 12 months, then deleted.</li>
        <li><b>Subscriber and account data</b> is kept while the account is open, and 6 months after you close it.</li>
        <li><b>Financial records</b>, once any exist, are kept 6 years, because HMRC requires it.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK GDPR you can ask us to show you what we hold, correct it, delete it, hand it over, or restrict what we do with it. <a href="mailto:privacy@joinourjam.com">Write to the privacy desk</a> and we will action it within one month.</p>
      <p>If we get it wrong, you can complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk">Information Commissioner’s Office</a>. We would rather you told us first.</p>
      <h2>7. Outside the UK</h2>
      <p>Some of these processors operate outside the UK. Where they do, transfers need a lawful mechanism. The mechanism for each one will be confirmed before launch. This page does not pretend that confirmation has happened.</p>
      <h2>8. Children</h2>
      <p>CITY JAM is not built for under-16s. If you are under 16, a parent or guardian needs to agree on your behalf. If we learn we are holding a child’s data without that, we delete it.</p>
      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes materially, we say what changed. No silent edits.</p>
      <h2>10. Talking to us</h2>
      <p><a href="mailto:privacy@joinourjam.com">Write to the privacy desk</a>. A person reads it.</p>
      <div class="acts">
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/terms">Terms</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/">Back to the room</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
